## The rule that breaks things if ignored

**Client components never import `lib/db.ts` or `lib/schema.ts`.**

`lib/db.ts` uses `drizzle-orm/neon-http`, which is fetch-based and pulls in
`@neondatabase/serverless`. Import it into anything under a `'use client'`
directive and the client bundle pulls the driver in and the page breaks at
runtime, not at build time.

```
server component ──▶ lib/api.ts ──▶ lib/db.ts ──▶ Neon
       └──▶ view models from lib/mappers.ts
client component ──▶ lib/client-api.ts (axios) ──▶ app/api/** ──▶ lib/api.ts
client component ──▶ lib/validation/*  (zod, safe both sides)
```

- `lib/api.ts` is the **only** module that queries. Nothing else calls `db.select`.
- It returns view models from `lib/mappers.ts`, never Drizzle rows.
- Server components fetch initial data and pass plain objects as props.

## The closed post-type union

Exactly 8 types, closed:

| kind | types | CSS |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `image` | `memory`, `achievement`, `mood`, `feeling`, `album` | `feed-post-<type>` |
| `literary` | `quote`, `poem`, `note` | `literary-card-<type>` |

`lib/post-types.ts` is the single source of truth — label, kind, blurb, image
rules, per-type zod shape. The `post_types` table is seeded from that same
constant, so the composer's dynamic form and the validator cannot drift. Adding a
type touches a closed union in three places and also needs the CSS rule, or the
card renders unstyled.

Rules that are easy to forget: `mood` and `feeling` require `moodScore` (1–10),
`album` requires 2–10 media, `note` rejects images, `quote` allows at most one.

## The no-database fallback is deliberate

`lib/db-safe.ts` returns `null` when `DATABASE_URL` is unset, and every reader in
`lib/api.ts` falls back to `lib/people.ts`. This is not laziness — `next build`
renders pages, so a hard database dependency breaks the build for anyone without
Neon configured. Writes return `503` with a clear message.

`lib/people.ts` is seed data plus that fallback, not the live data source.

## Uploads: three steps, and bytes never touch Next

```
POST /api/uploads/presign    → { key, uploadUrl, headers }
PUT  <uploadUrl>             → browser → MinIO directly
POST /api/uploads/complete   → creates the media row, returns mediaId
```

- The presigned key is server-generated `posts/<year>/<uuid>.<ext>`, extension
  derived from `contentType`, never from user input.
- Do not collapse this into a multipart upload for the public composer — that is
  what `/api/admin/upload` is for. The composer needs progress events.
- `complete` stays idempotent-safe: `409` if the key already has a row, `404` if
  the object is not in the bucket.
- Images come back through `GET /api/images/[...key]`, which streams from MinIO
  with `immutable` caching. The browser never sees `localhost:9000`, which keeps
  the bucket private and makes dev and production identical.
- `mediaUrl()` prefers `media.publicPath` over the MinIO key — that is how the
  seed reuses the existing 2 MB PNGs in `public/images/`. Reuse those assets;
  do not add new images to `public/`.
- Routes touching the `minio` SDK need `export const runtime = 'nodejs'`, and
  `next.config.mjs` sets `serverExternalPackages: ['minio']`.

## Auth: two unrelated systems

- Better Auth email/password — `lib/auth.ts`, catch-all `app/api/auth/[...all]`,
  schema from `pnpm dlx auth@latest generate` in `lib/auth-schema.ts`. Sign-up
  creates a linked `people` row (`people.userId`). `lib/session.ts` maps the
  Better Auth session to that profile for compose/star/upload.
- `biography_admin` — the dashboard, gated on `ADMIN_PASSWORD`.

Do not merge these. Authors sign in at `/login`; the dashboard stays separate.

## Styling is hand-written CSS

Tailwind v4 is installed and `@import 'tailwindcss'` is present, but **no page
uses a single utility class**. `className="flex gap-4 text-sm"` silently matches
nothing.

- Semantic classes in `app/globals.css`, written one rule per line with no blank
  lines between rules. Match that format exactly.
- Reuse `:root` variables: `--ink`, `--paper`, `--muted`, `--line`, `--serif`,
  `--sans`, `--mono`.
- The grayscale/serif editorial treatment is the design. No colour, no rounded
  corners, no shadows the neighbours lack.
- Small uppercase mono labels: `feed-kicker`, `section-kicker`,
  `profile-eyebrow`. State classes: `is-loaded`, `is-selected`, `is-active`.
- `app/dashboard/dashboard.css` is separate, imported by the dashboard page.
  `app/dashboard/dashboard.module.css` is dead — nothing imports it.
- `components/ui/button.tsx` is unused by every page; `cn()` in `lib/utils.ts`
  exists only for it. Do not reach for either.

## Verification

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit    # the ONLY type check
pnpm build          # typescript.ignoreBuildErrors is true, so this proves little
```

`next.config.mjs` sets `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors: true`, so **`next build`
succeeds even when types are broken**. Always run `npx tsc --noEmit`. There is no
lint script, no test framework, no CI config.

Package manager is pnpm. An untracked `package-lock.json` and an npm-installed
`node_modules` may be present; do not commit them, do not reinstall with npm.

Next 16 async request APIs — keep `await params` and `await cookies()`.

## Gotchas

- `components.json` declares a `@/hooks` alias, but no `hooks/` directory exists.
- `images.unoptimized: true` is set and every page uses plain `<img>`. Do not
  introduce `next/image`.
- `public/images/*.png` are roughly 2 MB each.
- `lib/db.ts` resolves the connection lazily — do not make it throw at import
  time, or the mock fallback dies with it.